# A home is a private repo: its Spark, its settings and its prompts are
# tracked, so every change to who it is has a history. What is below never is.

# The store. It changes every turn, it is binary, and git would keep every
# version whole forever. It leaves this machine as a nightly release asset
# instead (server/offsite.py), and every local copy sits in all_backups/.
data/store.db
data/store.db-journal
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal

# Every local copy: stamped zips, the latest zip, the night's before/after.
all_backups/

# What the room says while it runs.
logs/

# Keys: one per paired person, and the key to the angel door. Secrets with a
# long life never ride out with a push.
data/people/
data/angel.token
data/angel.inbox.json
data/push.json

# The room's running account of itself -- state, not history.
data/tray.json
data/watch_state.json
data/wakings.jsonl
data/comment_posts.jsonl
data/hands.json
data/overmind.json
data/overmind.tmp

# What hands did, step by step, and the checkouts they worked in. Big, and
# they ride in the backup zip rather than in git.
data/workers/
data/worktrees/

# Pictures shown to the assistant, and anything trained on its store. Its
# store's text, laid out another way -- they ride in the backup zip.
data/pictures/
data/adapter/
data/writer/

# Free notes: somebody's own scratch. They ride in the backup zip.
data/notes/
